 ****************************************************************  325 1451
           MODIFICATIONS FOR ENDF/B-VIII.0_beta-4                  325 1451
                       G. M. Hale (2/7/17)                         325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 Results from a new R-matrix analysis of the 7Li system, done up   325 1451
 to 4 MeV neutron energy, were included in this evaluation for     325 1451
 MF=3, MT=1,2,105.  The results were obtained by fitting the (n,t) 325 1451
 cross section that resulted from the 2016 GMA standards evalua-   325 1451
 tion, along with data from other reactions in the 7Li sytem.      325 1451
 The cross sections were joined at 3.8 MeV to the existing ENDF/B  325 1451
 VII.1 file, and the total cross section was re-summed to be con-  325 1451
 sistent with the partials (2+4+24+102+103+105) at all energies.   325 1451
 Covariances (MF=33), and a more detailed description will be ad-  325 1451
 ded to the file in a later version of ENDF/B-VIII.                325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 ****************************************************************  325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
          MODIFICATION OF ENDF/B-VII EVALUATION FOR NEW DATA       325 1451
                           G. M. Hale (3/9/09)                     325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
    Results of new R-matrix analysis that included absolute WNR    325 1451
    measurements of the 6Li(n,t)4He differential cross section     325 1451
    made in 2008 were used for MF=3, MT=105 above the standards    325 1451
    range (0.94 <= E <= 4) MeV.  In the range (4 <= E <= 8)        325 1451
    MeV, the (n,t) cross section was obtained from Legendre fits   325 1451
    to the new WNR data, matched smoothly to the previous cross    325 1451
    section above 8 MeV.  The differences with the previous (n,t)  325 1451
    cross section above about 1 MeV were distributed between the   325 1451
    elastic (MT=2) and inelastic (MT=58) cross sections, so that   325 1451
    the same total cross section was preserved.                    325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 ****************************************************************  325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
          MODIFICATION OF ENDF/B-VI EVALUATION FOR ENDF/B-VII      325 1451
                  G. M. Hale and P. G. Young (4/12/06)             325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 1. Standard cross sections for MT=105 from the ENDF/B-VII         325 1451
    international standards analysis were incorporated below       325 1451
    2.8 MeV. The previous evaluation (ENDF/B-VI) was smoothed      325 1451
    slightly between 2.8-3.4 MeV for a smooth join of the data.    325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 2. MF=4, MT=2 elastic angular distributions from the ENDF/B-VII   325 1451
    R-Matrix analysis were added below 2.8 MeV.                    325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 3. MF=6, MT=105 angular distributions were added from the         325 1451
    ENDF/B-VII R-Matrix analysis below 2.8 MeV.                    325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
 4. MF=33, MT=105 data from the ENDF/B-VII international           325 1451
    standards analysis were incorporated into the evaluation.      325 1451
                                                                   325 1451
